      "detail": "Ripe papaya flesh is soft and sweet and can be eaten as it is; the claim circulating online that papaya enlarges the breast has no basis, and eating fruit need not carry a burden of promised effects. Traditional food wisdom holds that ripe papaya is moistening, and in Guangdong it is used in autumn and winter for soups and for stewing with milk — what is wanted is that warm, gentle sweetness, not some mysterious efficacy: the online claim about the breast has no basis and is best taken as talk, for fruit need not carry a burden of promised effects. Green papaya is not suitable for eating raw, and as a vegetable it must be blanched or pickled according to a recipe and properly handled before it comes to the table. The seeds and the green skin are not eaten; half a ripe fruit at a time is enough, and the flesh closest to the skin is the sweetest. Choose a fully ripe one for a child — soft, sweet and no burden, a fruit the south has all year round and can be trusted."
